blic-documents/spl_1JSHTPPG11S0ZR1Z/prj_1JWX91R5E1S00PN0/pjd_1KPDB584D1S03R1M/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 17 Apr 2026\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KKVSMZ321S0C4CG?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JSHTPPG11S0ZR1Z/prj_1JWX91R5E1S00PN0/pjd_1KPDBCDAQ1S088P6/validation_%26_verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JSHTPPG11S0ZR1Z/prj_1JWX91R5E1S00PN0/pjd_1KPDB584D1S03R1M/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JSHTPPG11S0ZR1Z/prj_1JWX91R5E1S00PN0/pjd_1KPDB2JBZ1S0WEAA/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JSHTPPG11S0ZR1Z/prj_1JWX91R5E1S00PN0/pjd_1KG21Z37B1S0BV4D/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nBICRS\\n200Y+\\nProject Nandani\\nGround Up\\nISSUED\\n4.97\\nBUFFER POOL\\n0.1\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n08 Mar 2026 to 08 Mar 2031\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nFeedstocks\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nProject Nandani converts sugarcane residues into high-quality biochar through advanced pyrolysis in Maharashtra’s sugarcane belt, preventing open-field burning and enabling durable carbon storage. The project improves soil fertility and water retention, supports regenerative agriculture, and generates verified carbon removal credits under the Isometric Standard—linking climate action with rural livelihoods.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\nEnviance\\n->\\nProject code\\nPZDR\\nApproval date\\n17 Apr 2026\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.3\\nBaseline protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.1\\nSUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT GOALS\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nProject Nandani\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n17 Apr 2026\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 4.97 tCO₂e removed from Project Nandani on 16 Mar 2026\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n4.971 t\\nSequestrations\\n6.846 t\\n-\\nActivities\\n1.875 tCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nSugarcane Leaves and Tops\\tBiomass\\t17 Apr 2026\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n17 Apr 2026\\tValidation & Verification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n17 Apr 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n17 Apr 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n28 Jan 2026\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 4 of 4\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n4.97\\nRetired\\n0\\nBuffer pool\\n0.1\\nCrediting period\\n08 Mar 2026 to 08 Mar 2031\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n17 Apr 2026\\t4.97\\t0.1\\t4.87\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Ground Up's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 0.1 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 0.1 certificates.\\n\\nGround Up has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"